restrictive. It is not suitable for a public project that You want other people
to build on.

If You want that, use a real open source license — MIT, Apache-2.0, or
GPL-3.0 — and accept that credit becomes a request rather than a restriction.

This document is a plain-language contract, not legal advice. If a real dispute
ever arises, consult a lawyer in Your jurisdiction. In most countries the
automatic copyright You already hold on this work does most of the actual
enforcement work; this file mainly establishes that You said no clearly, in
writing, in advance.

